*
* setting up automated responses
hao clear
hao tgt HASP099
hao cmd script SCRIPTS/pjes2
hao tgt HASP085
hao cmd script SCRIPTS/zeod
hao tgt IEE334I
hao cmd script SCRIPTS/quiesce
hao tgt HHC00814I Processor CP00: SIGP Stop
hao cmd script SCRIPTS/poweroff
hao tgt HHC00814I Processor CP01: SIGP Stop
hao cmd script SCRIPTS/poweroff
# With NUMCPU 1 there is no SIGP Stop: MVS loads wait state CCC after QUIESCE
hao tgt HHC00809I Processor CP00: disabled wait state 000A0000 00000CCC
hao cmd script SCRIPTS/poweroff
hao tgt ([0-9]{2}) IKT010D 
hao cmd /R $1,FSTOP
# For information see https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/zos/2.3.0?topic=commands-mvs-system-reference
* Cancel the processing of all automatic commands.
/$CA,ALL 
pause 2
* Switching SMF
/SWITCH SMF
pause 2
* Preventing users from logging on
/MODIFY TSO,USERMAX=0
pause 2
* Stopping the servers: JES2 does not end while a started task runs,
* and a P for a task that is not running only gets IEE341I.
* One command per pause: the 3215 console keeps only the last line
* typed before MVS reads it.
/P FTPD
pause 1
/P HTTPD
pause 3
/P UFSD
pause 3
* Stop JES2 Initiators
/$PI
pause 2
* Stopping JES2
/$P PRT1  
/$P PRT2  
/$P PRT3  
/$P PUNCH1
/$P RDR1
/$P RDR2  
pause 3
* Shutting down TSO
/STOP TSO
pause 3
* Shutting down VTAM
/HALT net,quick
pause 3